# What of the repo is sent to the worker image build (worker.Dockerfile, context: the repo root).
# BuildKit uses this file instead of any .dockerignore, so DevOps owns it. An allow-list: nothing
# goes in unless listed, so no .env, venv, model cache or other department's files can be baked in.
*

# AI's code, prompts and the fixtures its fake backends read, plus the locked dependencies
!ai/core/
!ai/prompts/
!ai/tests/fixtures/
# The canned AnalyzedRequests and SkillSpecs that AI's FakePipeline returns (SKILLFORGE_PIPELINE=fake,
# the demo's fake LLM mode: docs/devops/demo-codespaces.md)
!ai/examples/
!ai/pyproject.toml
!ai/uv.lock

# The placeholder worker's check, and the entrypoint that reads the key from its secret file
!devops/docker/worker_check.py
!devops/docker/worker-entrypoint.sh

# Never, even inside the folders above
**/.env*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
